-- addendum (same day): the seat-map routing rule, from the decompile of FUN_140118950 and the first negative self-tests
UPSERT steam_routine:FUN_140118950 SET seat_routing='CONFIRMED by decompile 2026-09-03: the wrapper saves prev (+0x228..0x234), ZEROES pads +0x218..+0x224, then for k in 0..3 if seat(k) = *(game_state+0x258+4k) >= 0 writes pad[seat(k)] = inputs[k] & 0xFFFFFF. With the OFFLINE seat map {0,0,0,0} only inputs[3] reaches seat 0 (last write wins) and seat 1 is never fed: the first negative receipt self-tests (bits 0x8/0x1/0x40 on seat 0) changed 0 blk bytes over 20 ticks for that reason. A receipt must set {0,1,-1,-1} (player k -> seat k). Contract C2.';
UPSERT finding:determinism_contract SET note_c2='2026-09-03 correction: C2 requires the seat map game_state+0x258..0x264 = {0,1,-1,-1} for a two-player receipt (the wrapper zeroes the pads and routes inputs[k] only through seats >= 0); an offline anchor holds {0,0,0,0}. receipt_gate.py writes the map into the job.';

-- addendum 2 (same day): the entity list DAT_142edf628 (Track H falsification, docs/RECEIPT-PLAYER-G.md) and the battle-frame anchor carry list
UPSERT global:entity_list_head SET addr='0x142edf628', steam_off='DAT_142edf628', type='ptr', note='exe-global POINTER to the in-block entity table blk+0x324E0 (live 0x146f34e0 = blk+0x324E0); the table records +0x20+8k = blk+0x32500+8k hold the six ABSOLUTE fighter self-pointers blk+0x3DB8+n*0x738 in tag order (0,2,4,1,3,5 live). Read every tick by FUN_140634600 / FUN_14063b920 / FUN_14063bd70 / caseD_7 and by the save-slot sync FUN_140607e90 (Track H AV c0000005 at 0x1406083be dereferencing entity[+0x20] after a blk-only anchor restore: the pointers belonged to the source process). Static per match, process-absolute: a loader must set it to blk_new+0x324E0 and relocate the six self-pointers by blk_new - blk_old. The seven qwords 0x142edf630..0x142edf667 point at stage POL models DC 0x0D82D210 / 0x0D83A6A8 / 0x0D83AA48 / 0x0D83ADE8 / 0x0D83C380 / 0x0D83D710 / 0x0D83EAA0 (AFS 801+2*id); nothing else in 0x142edf600..0x142edf800 is touched by the tick. CONFIRMED by trace + live image 2026-09-03.';
UPSERT finding:determinism_battle_anchor_carry SET status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-09-03', contribution_candidate=true, note='WHAT A BATTLE-FRAME ANCHOR MUST CARRY (and how the heap entities become valid in a target process): (1) blk[0..0x33B18) relocated by blk_new-blk_old on the six self-pointers blk+0x32500+8k (self-check: a permutation of blk+0x3DB8+n*0x738), on ctx+0x1f81b0 (= blk) and on every in-block absolute; the 557 asset pointers of a battle block point into the PL images and relocate by dcram_new-dcram_old; (2) the game_state page 0x140ac6d40+0x1000 (+0x10 frame fn, +0x1B0/+0x1B8, +0x208 staging, +0x218.. pads, +0x258.. seat map {0,1,-1,-1}, +0x758 picks (not read by the tick: match-init input only), +0x828/+0x520/+0x80C gates); (3) the exe page 0x142edf300..0x142edf700 (NOT ..0x600): DAT_142edf560/580 rewritten to the new base, DAT_142edf588/590/598 and 0x142edf630..0x667 rebased into the DC-RAM image, DAT_142edf628 = blk_new+0x324E0, the 0x142edf543/546 HUD state; (4) ctx: the texture-slot table ctx+0x1e0030..0x1e31CC and the balanced matrix state, ctx+8 = dcram_new; (5) DC-RAM: the six PL images (AFS 209+cid + tail) and the effects/HUD/stage banks. Every entity the tick dereferences lives in blk or in the DC-RAM image; nothing on the tick path points into a Windows heap except the debug ring *(DAT_142ebc010)+0x34AAC (no effect) and the UCRT ptd (rebuilt). The p-code harness is this experiment with delta = 0 and passes; the two-process case is the open falsification (receipt_gate.py on a restored battle-frame anchor).';
RELATE finding:determinism_battle_anchor_carry->about:det_about_28->global:entity_list_head;
